.TH sacdfs 1  sacdfs sacdfs
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
sacdfs \- Read\-only FUSE filesystem that shows SACD disc images as DSF files, decoded on demand
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsacdfs\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-foreground\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-cache\-mb\fR] [\fB\-\-listing\-mb\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-burst\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-burst\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-pauses\fR] [\fB\-\-pcm\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-pcm\-cutoff\fR] [\fB\-\-pcm\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-multichannel\-album\-suffix\fR] [\fB\-\-tags\fR] [\fB\-\-musicbrainz\fR] [\fB\-\-flatten\fR] [\fB\-\-sidecars\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-other\fR] [\fB\-\-index\-cache\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-open\-images\fR] [\fB\-\-request\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-stop\-grace\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fISOURCE\fR> <\fIMOUNTPOINT\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the audio of SACD disc images as DSF and WAV files, decoded on demand.
.PP
SOURCE is an image file or a directory searched recursively for *.iso files. Each image appears as MOUNTPOINT/<relative dir>/<image name>/{Stereo,Multichannel}/NN \- title.dsf, with NN \- title.wav (24\-bit PCM, converted on demand) next to it. Unmount with `umount MOUNTPOINT` as root, else `fusermount3 \-u MOUNTPOINT` (`fusermount \-u` with FUSE 2), or stop sacdfs with SIGINT, SIGTERM or SIGHUP (it exits after \-\-stop\-grace seconds even if files are still open).
.PP
`sacdfs verify SOURCE [EXTRACTS]...` checks extracted DSF and DFF files against what sacdfs serves, before they are deleted: see `sacdfs verify \-\-help`. `sacdfs tags` keeps user tags for the files (`\-\-tags`): see `sacdfs tags \-\-help`.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-foreground\fR
Stay in the foreground and log to standard error
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 0]
DST decoder threads (0: one per CPU; under a memory limit, at most one per 64 MiB of it, and at least 2)
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-mb\fR \fI<N>\fR
Size of the cache of decoded and converted frames, in MiB (default: 32, or 16 under a memory limit below 256 MiB)
.TP
\fB\-\-listing\-mb\fR \fI<N>\fR
Memory kept for what listed images hold (their TOCs and files), in MiB; past it, those not used lately are read again when next used. 0: no bound (default: no bound, or 3/8 of the memory limit under one)
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-burst\fR \fI<X>\fR [default: 3.5]
How fast players read a track they start, in times real time (#504). Where this machine decodes a format slower than that (measured as it serves), a starting track is decoded ahead without waiting for the player\*(Aqs reads. 0: off
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-burst\-secs\fR \fI<SECS>\fR [default: 8]
Seconds of audio decoded ahead when a track starts playing, within a quarter of the cache
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<LIST>\fR [default: dsf,wav]
Which files to show: dsf, wav, or both (dsf,wav)
.TP
\fB\-\-pauses\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: dropped]
Pauses: dropped (the default: each file is the track\*(Aqs own range) or kept (each file is the track with its pause, as extractors that keep pauses write it)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
dropped
.IP \(bu 2
kept
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-pcm\-rate\fR \fI<HZ>\fR [default: 176400]
Sample rate of the WAV files, in Hz: 88200, 176400 or 352800
.TP
\fB\-\-pcm\-cutoff\fR \fI<KHZ>\fR [default: 40]
Low\-pass cutoff of the PCM conversion: 40 or 30 (kHz), or wide (about 80 kHz; needs a \-\-pcm\-rate of 176400 or 352800)
.TP
\fB\-\-pcm\-gain\fR \fI<DB>\fR [default: 0]
Gain of the PCM conversion in dB, \-60 to +24; samples that would clip are clamped
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-multichannel\-album\-suffix\fR
Do not add " (Multichannel)" to the album tag of the files of the multichannel area (by default they get it, so players and servers show them as an album of their own)
.TP
\fB\-\-tags\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory of tags files (#81), one per disc, named by its disc key (`sacdfs tags key IMAGE`): their tags override and add to the TOC\*(Aqs. Without it, or for a disc without a file, the files are as the TOC gives them
.TP
\fB\-\-musicbrainz\fR[=\fI<LOOKUPS>\fR]
Look up, on MusicBrainz, discs without a track title, album or artist, in the background, and write what matches to the \-\-tags directory (which must be writable), as `sacdfs tags fetch` does: by barcode or catalogue number, confirmed by track count, durations and ISRCs. Off by default; nothing else in a mount uses the network. At most 1 request per second, once per disc; no client request waits for it.

Takes `=LOOKUPS`, `name`, `durations` or both (`name,durations`), to try more when that finds nothing: `name` also searches by album and artist, from the disc\*(Aqs text or the image\*(Aqs path (sends those names); `durations` also asks by the tracks\*(Aq start times (a disc of 4 tracks or more; sends the times).
.TP
\fB\-\-flatten\fR
Collapse each chain of folders below the top level that holds a single image into its outermost folder, which then holds the image\*(Aqs Stereo/Multichannel folders
.TP
\fB\-\-sidecars\fR \fI<LIST>\fR [default: default]
Files passed through from SOURCE, byte for byte, next to the images\*(Aq folders: a comma\-separated list of extensions and folder names ending in / (whose whole content passes). `default` is jpg,jpeg,png,webp,m3u,m3u8,Artwork/,Scans/; `\-item` removes an item (default,\-webp), `none` passes nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-other\fR[=\fI<yes|no>\fR]
Let other users read the mount: the default when run as root (the mount is read\-only). A user other than root needs `user_allow_other` in /etc/fuse.conf for it
.TP
\fB\-\-index\-cache\fR \fI<DIR|off>\fR
Directory of the persistent seek index, which lets seeks after a remount skip most of their search (default: $XDG_CACHE_HOME/sacdfs, else ~/.cache/sacdfs). `off`: keep none, so that every mount starts with an empty one
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-open\-images\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 64]
Most image files kept open at once (1 to 1024); the least recently used is closed first, and any closes after 5 minutes unused
.TP
\fB\-\-request\-timeout\fR \fI<SECS>\fR [default: 30]
Seconds a request (a read, a lookup, a listing) may wait for the source before it fails with an I/O error and a log line, so that a stalled share never hangs a client; 0 waits for good
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\-grace\fR \fI<SECS>\fR [default: 10]
Seconds after SIGINT, SIGTERM or SIGHUP that sacdfs keeps serving files clients still hold open before it exits anyway (the mount is detached at once, so nothing new opens); those clients then get I/O errors. 0 waits for the last file to close, however long
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Append the log to FILE instead of standard error, at info level unless \-v says more. Without it a background mount logs nowhere, except to the journal under systemd
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Log more (repeat for more still); RUST_LOG overrides it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fISOURCE\fR>
An SACD image file, or a directory of them
.TP
<\fIMOUNTPOINT\fR>
A directory to mount on, normally empty (its files are hidden while mounted); not SOURCE or a directory above it
.SH "MOUNT OPTIONS"
.B mount \-t fuse.sacdfs
runs
.B sacdfs SOURCE MOUNTPOINT \-o OPTIONS .
Each long option above is an
.B \-o
option with the dashes written as underscores:
.BR allow_other ,
.BR cache_mb=64 ,
.BR pcm_rate=88200 ,
.BR flatten ,
.BR tags=/etc/sacdfs/tags ,
.BR index_cache=off ,
.BR verbose=2 .
A comma separates
.B \-o
options, so a list value uses
.B +
instead:
.BR format=dsf+wav ,
.BR sidecars=default+cue ,
.BR musicbrainz=name+durations .
The options of
.BR mount (8)
and fstab (\c
.BR ro ,
.BR noauto ,
.BR nofail ,
.BR _netdev ,
.BR nosuid ,
.BR nodev ,
.B x\-systemd.*
and similar) are accepted and ignored: sacdfs is always read\-only. Any other option is an error.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
The mount ended normally (a background mount returns once the filesystem is mounted).
.TP
.B 1
The mount failed, or an option or a folder was refused; the one line on standard error says why
and what to type.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (an unknown option or a missing argument).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Overrides the level set by
.BR \-v ,
for example
.BR RUST_LOG=sacdfs=debug ,
or
.B RUST_LOG=info,sacdfs::trace=debug
for the read trace without the rest of the debug log.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Where the seek index lives by default:
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/sacdfs ,
else
.IR ~/.cache/sacdfs .
.TP
.B FUSERMOUNT_PATH
The FUSE mount helper to use, instead of
.B fusermount3
or
.BR fusermount .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/sacdfs
The persistent seek index (see
.BR \-\-index\-cache ).
Deleting it is always safe.
.TP
.I /etc/fuse.conf
Needs the line
.B user_allow_other
for
.B \-\-allow\-other
by a user other than root.
.TP
.I /etc/sysconfig/sacdfs
.TQ
.I /etc/default/sacdfs
The settings of the packaged systemd unit and of
.BR sacdfs\-ctl (8):
the first in the RPM, the second in the deb package and the release archive.
.SH EXAMPLES
A one\-off mount in the foreground, with a log:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sacdfs \-f \-v /srv/sacd /mnt/sacd
.fi
.RE
.PP
Unmount it with
.B umount /mnt/sacd
as root, else
.BR "fusermount3 \-u /mnt/sacd" .
.PP
An fstab line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
/srv/sacd  /mnt/sacd  fuse.sacdfs  ro,allow_other,format=dsf,_netdev,nofail  0 0
.fi
.RE
.PP
A systemd unit (the packages ship a hardened one, which reads
.IR /etc/sysconfig/sacdfs ):
.PP
.RS
.nf
[Service]
Type=notify
CacheDirectory=sacdfs
ExecStart=/usr/bin/sacdfs \-f \-\-index\-cache %C/sacdfs /srv/sacd /mnt/sacd
Restart=on\-failure
.fi
.RE
.PP
The container image on a NAS, which mounts and shares over SMB and NFS (tuning is set through
its environment variables, such as
.BR SACDFS_CACHE_MB ):
.PP
.RS
.nf
docker run \-d \-\-name sacdfs \-\-restart unless\-stopped \e
  \-\-device /dev/fuse \-\-cap\-drop ALL \e
  \-\-cap\-add SYS_ADMIN \-\-cap\-add DAC_OVERRIDE \-\-cap\-add DAC_READ_SEARCH \e
  \-\-cap\-add SETUID \-\-cap\-add SETGID \-\-cap\-add NET_BIND_SERVICE \-\-cap\-add SETPCAP \e
  \-\-security\-opt no\-new\-privileges:true \-\-security\-opt apparmor=unconfined \e
  \-p 445:445 \-p 2049:2049 \-v /path/to/images:/images:ro \-v sacdfs\-cache:/cache sacdfs
.fi
.RE
.PP
Look discs up on MusicBrainz in the background, writing tags files to a folder:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sacdfs \-\-tags ~/sacd\-tags \-\-musicbrainz=name,durations ~/sacd\-images ~/sacd
.fi
.RE
.SH "DEPRECATED OPTIONS"
These still work, on the command line, as
.B \-o
options and in
.BR SACDFS_OPTIONS ,
and log one line naming the new form. They are kept through 1.0 at least.
.TP
.B \-\-lookup\-name
Use
.BR \-\-musicbrainz=name .
.TP
.B \-\-lookup\-durations
Use
.BR \-\-musicbrainz=durations .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-allow\-other
Use
.BR \-\-allow\-other=no .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-index\-cache
Use
.BR "\-\-index\-cache off" .
